  "term": "technical term",
  "definition": "In historical psychology and philosophy, active powers referred to the capacities of impulse, desire, and will that move a person to act, contrasted with intellectual or cognitive powers such as reasoning and judging. The source also notes that this expression is no longer used as a technical term.",
